  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-057",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Pre-move cut share (vs drive share) predicts whether a connector's organizational function reproduces after a move. Specifically, Cut share rho=+0.265 p=0.011 AUC 0.653. Cut-drive rho=+0.314 p=0.002 AUC 0.656. Drive rho=-0.278 p=0.007. Top cut tercile 65% portable median Delta +0.167; bottom 35% median -0.039. LOO AUC 0.622; permutation p=0.005."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-090",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "A study on connector diet matching to destination structural gaps found the binary match rate was 15.7%. For taxonomy CONNECTORS, delta match vs mismatch medians were +0.540 vs +0.069 (p=0.156, n=5/14). The all-movers binary result (p=0.0283) did not hold as a continuous Spearman (-0.034)."
