 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "The 'n=24 units' is critically vague. If this refers to players, it is almost certainly too small to reliably define distinct 'cut-heavy' and 'drive-heavy' shaper groups, observe sufficient movers within each group, and detect a statistically significant difference in portability after controlling for confounders. Historical evidence consistently points to this as a major limitation for mover studies."
  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "A player's success in a new role or team is confounded by numerous factors including the quality of the new team, coaching philosophy, available talent, player age, injury history, and the specific 'fit' of their skills with the new team's needs. Without controlling for these, any observed effect could be spurious."
