  "supported": 0.3,
  "rejected": 0.1,
  "untestable": 0.5,
  "artifact": 0.05,
  "uncertain": 0.05
 },
 "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "The difference in the probability of 'role reproduction' (or a suitable proxy for 'traveling better') for 'cut-heavy shapers' compared to 'drive-heavy shapers' after a team change, controlling for pre-move player quality, destination team quality, and other confounders.",
  "unit": "Player-move instance. Each time a 'shaper' player changes teams, it constitutes one unit of observation. The 'n=24 units' must be clarified to refer to player-move instances.",
  "sample": "All players classified as 'shapers' (based on a predefined set of offensive actions and usage) who changed teams between the 2022-23 and 2025-26 NBA seasons. Players will be categorized as 'cut-heavy' or 'drive-heavy' based on their pre-move offensive play-type distribution (e.g., top/bottom tercile of cut-to-drive ratio among shapers). A minimum of 30 player-move instances per group (cut-heavy, drive-heavy) is targeted for a minimally powered analysis; if this cannot be met with the 'n=24 units', the project will be re-evaluated for feasibility.",
  "power": "Target 80% power to detect a medium effect size (e.g., Cohen's h = 0.5 for proportions or r = 0.3 for correlations) in role reproduction between cut-heavy and drive-heavy shapers, assuming a two-tailed alpha of 0.05. This requires a precise definition of the outcome and an estimate of variance. If the sample size is severely limited (e.g., <30 per group), a power analysis will be conducted to determine the minimum detectable effect (MDE), and the decision may revert to 'do_not_proceed' if the MDE is too large to be practically meaningful.",
  "controls": "Pre-move player quality (e.g., prior season's efficiency metrics, role usage, age), destination team quality (e.g., previous season's win rate, net rating, talent level), and potentially coaching scheme compatibility. Regression analysis (e.g., logistic regression for binary outcomes, linear regression for continuous outcomes) will be used to control for these variables.",
  "falsification": "The hypothesis would be falsified if there is no statistically significant difference in role reproduction between cut-heavy and drive-heavy shapers, or if drive-heavy shapers show significantly better role reproduction, after controlling for confounders. A non-significant result with adequate power (i.e., observed effect below MDE) would also be considered falsification of a meaningful effect.",
  "multiplicity": "No multiple primary hypotheses will be tested. If multiple outcome metrics for 'role travel' are considered, one primary outcome will be pre-specified, and others will be treated as exploratory. If multiple definitions of 'shapers' or 'cut/drive-heavy' are explored, appropriate multiplicity corrections (e.g., Bonferroni, FDR) will be applied or analyses will be designated as exploratory.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis is supported if the estimated effect (e.g., odds ratio, regression coefficient) for 'cut-heavy' shapers demonstrates significantly better role reproduction than 'drive-heavy' shapers (p < 0.05, one-tailed if directional hypothesis is retained, or two-tailed if exploring either direction) and the effect size is practically meaningful.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 regular seasons and playoffs. Play-by-play data, substitution data, box-score summaries, defensive matchup data, and derived play-type possession records from the graph database will be used."
 }
}

